          "links": null
        }
      ],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Follows the stem-chain sketch: one split per stage, each handing the rest of the\nsignal to the next one.\n\nFull Mixed Song -> split -> vocals + instrumental\n  vocals        -> VoxMain and VoxBacking, one ensemble each\n  instrumental  -> Drums  -> the kit: kick, snare, hats (+ toms, ride, crash, not saved)\n                     |            bongos, shakers, tambourine and Other Percs are described\n                     |            to SAM-Audio, which pulls a named sound out of anything\n                     v\n                  no drums -> bass -> no bass -> htdemucs_6s -> guitar, piano, Other\n                                                  strings and brass are described to SAM-Audio\n\nWhere the diagram and the library do not meet:\n  kick / snare / hats   the kit model's own names: kick, snare, toms, hh, ride, crash.\n                        It does not output bongos, shakers, tambourine or Other Percs.\n  bongos / shakers /    described to SAM-Audio and pulled out of the drums stem, which is\n  tambourine / Percs    what the diagram asks for and what the library can do\n  strings / brass       no model in the library targets either one; SAM-Audio is asked for\n                        them by name, from the same signal the chain carried past bass\n  guitar / piano        htdemucs_6s, the only model that produces them, in one pass\n  Other                 htdemucs_6s's own other stem\n\nEvery stage below the first split is fed the previous stage's remainder, so leftovers add up\ndown the chain. Feed them all the same instrumental instead if the drums or bass start to\nsound eaten."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
